## Scope and evidence

This review uses the support KB export dated 2026-10-04 and the course's
engineering update supplied by the student. The [original incident](/kb/incidents/4471) says that one fix
will cover the merged ticket. The executable classification identifies
different mechanisms, so that statement should not guide triage without review.

Counts below deduplicate report IDs before filtering to this ticket. Intake
tags are guesses from browser locale; the classifier uses tenant locale,
booking form version, and intake channel. Neither an intake tag nor a matching
subject proves that reports have the same cause.

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

## Shared parser

The shared parser reads day-first input as month-first. For example, R-41200
describes 7 April becoming 4 July, and R-41201 describes the reverse swap.
The classifier assigns day-first tenants' reports to this mechanism except
for booking-v3 form submissions.

Track the parser separately. Verify an explicit locale-aware date contract,
ambiguous dates, day values above twelve, and each supported intake channel.
Do not promise that this fix resolves every report in the classifier group.

## Booking form hint

Booking-v3 prints `MM/DD/YYYY` while interpreting submissions according to
the day-first tenant convention. Following the displayed hint can therefore
produce a different date. The affected form submissions belong to Alder
Physio, Copper Studio, and Pale Harbour; examples include R-41230, R-41241,
and R-41251.

Track this mechanism independently of the shared parser. Derive the displayed
hint and the accepted interpretation from the same contract, and test
booking-v3 forms with ambiguous input such as `04/07`.

## Unresolved symptoms

Desk notes flag R-41202, R-41209, R-41236, R-41344, and R-41620. Their bodies
mention adjacent weekdays, a June-only shift, an invite preceding a booking,
and different weekdays in Lisbon and Toronto. The current classifier assigns
them to parser by tenant; it does not examine those symptoms.

Retain their existing counted membership until evidence supports a different
classification. Check the original timestamps, intended local dates, time
zones, and event history before asserting another root cause or a report
count for it. Do not discard these reports because the ticket is marked known.

## Triage and queue history

The subject-based [triage page](/kb/triage/dedupe) and
[accepted decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject) disagree with
the cause-based explorer. Different subjects can describe the same mechanism,
and identical subjects can describe different ones.

<DedupeExplorer />

Investigate the mechanism before merging, and keep uncertain reports visible.
This draft does not rewrite the accepted decision or claim to enact a new
policy. A reviewed replacement decision is required to change that policy.

Received time and merge time describe different events. Use both to understand
the backlog rather than treating the merge date as the incident start.

<QueueTimeline ticket={4471} />

## Tracking status

The exported classifier groups now have separate public tracking issues:

- [Shared date parser](https://github.com/mth-b/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/1).
- [Booking-v3 form hint](https://github.com/mth-b/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/2).

The course's engineering update states that support ticket #4471 closed on
5 October with different outcomes for the two mechanisms:

| Mechanism | Desk outcome | Evidence from the update | Tracking disposition |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Parser | Fixed | `fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu locales` | Close as completed |
| Form hint | Won't fix | `booking-v3 form retired` | Close as not planned |

Retiring the form is not a hint correction. Do not describe both issues as
fixed merely because their parent ticket closed. The production change was
reported by the desk, not implemented or independently tested in this repository.
The unresolved symptoms above remain investigation leads; the update does
not establish their root causes.

